    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit so that creating an owner is rejected with **HTTP 429** once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`rest/advice/DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` thrown when the daily limit is reached, mirroring the existing `CityAtCapacityException` pattern.\n\n2. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` that returns `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) with a `ProblemDetail` body naming the `registrationDate` field in its `errors` array, consistent with the other handlers.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT = 100` constant and a `rejectDailyOwnerLimit()` method that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the current date and throws when the count is \u2265 100 (the count excludes the owner being created). It's invoked in `addOwner` right after required-field validation.\n\nVerification: the new acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, expect the 101st to be `429`) passes, and `./mvnw test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with all tests green.",
